From: "D.R.racer" <drracer@seznam.cz>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 15:57:50 +0200
Subject: ARM: dts: sun7i: add the external 32k crystal

Describe the optional 32.768 kHz crystal next to osc32k, the way the
A23/A33, A31 and H3/H5 device trees do, so that boards fitted with it
can hand it to the RTC. Nothing references it yet, so no board changes.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun7i-a20.dtsi | 12 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun7i-a20.dtsi b/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun7i-a20.dtsi
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun7i-a20.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun7i-a20.dtsi
@@ -218,6 +218,18 @@ osc32k: clk-32k {
 			clock-output-names = "osc32k";
 		};
 
+		/*
+		 * Optional 32.768 kHz crystal. Boards that have
+		 * it hand it to the RTC, which then runs LOSC from it.
+		 */
+		ext_osc32k: ext-osc32k-clk {
+			#clock-cells = <0>;
+			compatible = "fixed-clock";
+			clock-frequency = <32768>;
+			clock-accuracy = <50000>;
+			clock-output-names = "ext-osc32k";
+		};
+
 		/*
 		 * The following two are dummy clocks, placeholders
 		 * used in the gmac_tx clock. The gmac driver will
-- 
